    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** (74.74) stands as the clear anchor of the Austin Waves lineup. Despite a slight efficiency penalty due to the elite hold-out capability of the opposition, his dynamic platoon advantage against Soriano provides the highest ceiling on the board. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.24) and **Josh Lowe** (69.56) are our next most vital assets; the former benefits from a strong BvP track record and a high-leverage spot in the #2 hole, while **Josh Lowe** thrives against a vulnerable Gibson, whose 5.27 xERA creates a target-rich environment for our bats. We are leaning heavily into the Gibson matchup, as **Nolan Schanuel** (64.82) also clears the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold by capitalizing on his leadoff placement and the favorable matchup.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Jacob Wilson** (54.51), who fell just shy of cracking the starting nine. While **Jacob Wilson** posted a respectable score, he was squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-efficiency matchups against Gibson, which favored the inclusion of **Wade Meckler** (54.93) and **Denzer Guzman** (53.37). Our bench remains deep with options like **Miguel Vargas** and **Josh Jung**, but their lower relative efficiency\u2014compounded by less favorable order placement\u2014kept them on the pine. Notably, **Nasim Nunez** was avoided despite his speed profile because the combination of a bottom-tier batting order (#9) and a high-efficiency defensive catcher significantly capped his stolen base expectation. \n\nManagement should remain alert to the performance of **Andy Pages** (49.09), who carries the highest risk on the day. Facing Ryan with a negative 19% SP skill adjustment makes **Andy Pages** a fringe start, as his base efficiency is dragged down by the quality of the opposing arm. We are also monitoring **Jackson Merrill** (53.03); his dynamic platoon penalty against P\u00e9rez is significant, though his spot in the #5 hole provides enough insulation to avoid a total benching. Ensure that the late-afternoon weather reports do not shift, as any rain delays could impact the bullpen usage for the teams we are looking to exploit.",
